      "fragment_index": 2,
      "start": 57.91,
      "end": 130.15,
      "duration": 72.24,
      "text": "Let me also add in with an explanation, Shamir Ahmed. AI systems as social techno systems, so are deeply tied to social and economic structures. If those structures are unsustainable, AI will not only generate new inventions but also replicate and intensify existing harms. A crucial learning from our projects on big data and adaptive management and on Earth observation in agriculture is that poorly governed data systems can exasperate exclusion, surveillance or misallocation, especially when scaled via AI. With heavy dependency on external data sets and minimal local control and weak institutional capacity in data ownership and calibration, AI risks reinforcing dependency rather than building resilience. However, when AI is designed around inclusive and sustainable principles, it can do the opposite, challenging harmful structures rather than reinforcing them.",
