      "fragment_index": 3,
      "start": 130.15,
      "end": 201.2,
      "duration": 71.05,
      "text": "An example is our project on inclusive hiring and digital skills development, which counted systemic unemployment and exclusion by demonstrating how AI can make hiring practices fairer and digital skills more accessible. Another example is the inaugural AI and data science boot camp, where we built AI literacy amongst underrepresented groups to help redress intersectional gender imbalances and broaden participation in digital economies. So these slides or these examples show that while AI systems can mirror and reinforce inequitable social and economic models, they also hold the potential to challenge them. By embedding fairness, access and inclusion into design and deployment, AI can shift from reproducing systemic harms to actively redressing them, turning a source of risk into a lever of equity and empowerment.",
