      "fragment_index": 4,
      "start": 201.2,
      "end": 278.4,
      "duration": 77.2,
      "text": "As AI and data driven systems expand, people risk being reduced to mere data points, feeding distant algorithms. The future of human dependency, sorry, the future of human agency depends on shifting this dynamic. Communities themselves must shape the questions asked, the data collected and the decisions made. This means embedding participation, accountability and local knowledge into AI design so that technology strengthens our autonomy rather than eroding it. The United Nations recognized me with a solution is a strong illustration of community driven AI. By crowdsourcing real-time weather data, it shifts communities from being passive recipients of forecasts to active contributors. This not only strengthens local resilience but also enhances early warning and disaster preparedness, showing how AI can embed participation and deliver tangible public good outcomes.",
