      "fragment_index": 5,
      "start": 278.4,
      "end": 337.98,
      "duration": 59.58,
      "text": "Indeed, Mina, and I'd also like to add that without decolonial approaches, AI risks repeating extractive patterns just under a new shiny label of a green digital transition. Mina, in your participation at the Internet Governance Forum in 2024, as a panelist, you also stressed the need for decolonial AI governance. Yes, Shamirah. I also highlighted the need for stricter regulations and sustainability metrics to mitigate environmental harm. Warning that otherwise the so-called green digital transition could reproduce the same inequities under a new label. Essentially, the three examples you've shown highlight that sustainability is an standalone feature. It's woven into the other themes. This reminds me of what I've seen in our other global governance challenges or efforts for plastics.",
